        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Return Installment Analyst Result",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "let data = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_FOR_OBJECT_FETCH_LOOP.$output;\n\nlet sequence = 1;\n\nlet summary =  $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_SUMMARIZER.$output;\n\nlet recommendations = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_GENERATE_RECOMMENDATIONS.$output;\n\n\nlet output = [];\n\noutput.push({  \n    \"type\": \"text\",\n    \"content\": summary.replace(/\\n/g, '<br>'),\n    \"sequence\": sequence++\n});\n\ndata.forEach(dataFetched => {\n    try {\n        let toPush = JSON.parse(dataFetched).result;\n        toPush.sequence = sequence++;\n        output.push(toPush);\n     } catch (e) {\n        // Do nothing if JSON.parse fails; output remains unchanged.\n     }\n});\n\nif(recommendations.length > 0){\n  output.push({\n        \"type\": \"actions\",\n        \"heading\": \"Recommendations\",\n        \"content\": recommendations,\n        \"sequence\": sequence++\n    });\n}\n\n\nreturn output;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_CODE_RETURN_INSTALLMENT_ANALYST_RESULT",
          "id": "1772705437003",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-5 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Elaborate"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1773062450864"
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_ELABORATE",
          "id": "1773062152101",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773062152101_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "--- BEGIN PROMPT ---\nRewrite the user’s message into a concise, functionally precise request that downstream nodes can act on, without changing the original intent. Abstract all global rules and include only those that are applicable to this specific user query. Resolve flow-specific routing here when needed so downstream nodes can execute without re-deriving business policy. Do not include any technical id fields in outputs. Treat supplier number as a technical identifier, not a business-facing display field, unless the user explicitly asks for it.\n\nInputs\n- User Input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nAvailable Shapes\n- payablesSelectedInstallmentsSummary: {{$context.$variables.payablesSelectedInstallmentsSummary}}\n- payablesPaymentScheduleDetail: {{$context.$variables.payablesPaymentScheduleDetail}}\n- selectedPaymentInstallments: {{$context.$variables.selectedPaymentInstallments}}\n- paymentRunInstallments: {{$context.$variables.paymentRunInstallments}}\n- payablesUnselectedInstallments: {{$context.$variables.payablesUnselectedInstallments}}\n- payablesPaymentProcessRequest: {{$context.$variables.payablesPaymentProcessRequest}}\n\nFunctional context\n- Disbursement bank account: Internal company bank account used to disburse funds (payment origin).\n- External bank account: Payee/supplier bank account that receives the funds (payment destination).\n- Destination country in payment/document asks: The country of the external bank account (payment destination), not the disbursement bank account or legal entity country.\n\nFunctional rules\n- PPR/payment routing and scope\n  - “Installments under/related to a PPR” means selected-installment scope by default, but do not assume the data lives only in AP-stage selected installments.\n  - Selected row-level details are status-aware:\n    - AP-stage statuses (e.g., Selection in Progress, Selected, Validation in AP): use selectedPaymentInstallments.\n    - IBY-stage statuses (e.g., Formatting, Transmission, Confirmed/Paid): use paymentRunInstallments.\n    - Unknown/missing status: UNION selectedPaymentInstallments and paymentRunInstallments and deduplicate by business keys.\n  - For plain installment requests under a PPR where the lifecycle stage/status is not explicitly resolved, set Source to `selected installments + payment run installments (deduplicate)` so both AP-stage and IBY-stage selected-installment records are covered.\n  - Include unselected installments only if the user explicitly requests unselected items.\n  - When the user explicitly asks for installments, documents, or related records that are “stuck due to failure”, “stuck because of failure”, or “stuck in failure”, preserve that narrower intent as `Filters: stuck due to failure` rather than the broader `PPR failure statuses` family.\n  - When the user asks for installments, documents, or related records that have “failed in payment”, “failed”, “error”, or similar failure-state wording without the explicit “stuck” wording, preserve that as `Filters: PPR failure statuses` rather than inventing free-form status text.\n  - If the user names one specific PPR status meaning or code and that meaning maps unambiguously to a single lookup code in local shape metadata, preserve the exact lookup code in `Filters:` instead of the broader `PPR failure statuses` family. For example, preserve `failed document validation` as `Filters: PPR status code = VALIDATION_FAILED`.\n  - The `stuck due to failure` driver family is narrower than `PPR failure statuses`: it captures installments or documents that are blocked in failure-related review or payment-instruction states, not every record that has already failed in payment.\n  - The `payablesPaymentProcessRequest` driver topic `PPR fail statuses` belongs to the IBY-stage lifecycle. For installment or document requests filtered to `PPR failure statuses`, resolve the source to `payment run installments` unless the user explicitly asks for the PPR objects themselves.\n  - The `stuck due to failure` driver family also belongs to the IBY-stage lifecycle. For installment or document requests filtered to `stuck due to failure`, resolve the source to `payment run installments` unless the user explicitly asks for the PPR objects themselves.\n  - If the user explicitly asks for documents, use paymentRunInstallments (not installments).\n  - Prefer payment currency over invoice currency when amounts are shown in PPR/payment contexts.\n  - Do not default to selectedPaymentInstallments for PPR rollups without first resolving PPR status or applying the UNION fallback when status is unknown.\n- Supplier-level rollups under a PPR (apply when the user asks for supplier counts/totals for a given PPR)\n  - Resolve the data source using the status-aware routing above (AP→selectedInstallments; IBY→paymentRunInstallments; Unknown→UNION).\n  - If the user asks for both supplier counts and monetary totals, request one grouped supplier summary by supplier and payment currency so count and amount stay in the same result set.\n  - For any ask that includes installment count, treat an installment as the business-key combination of invoiceId + installmentNumber, not either field alone and not raw duplicate rows.\n  - Compute per supplier/payment-currency group:\n    - Count of installments via aggregation.\n    - If totals are requested, sum payment amounts with payment currency preference and format as <amount> <CURRENCY_CODE>.\n- Disbursement bank account handling\n  - For virtual card payments, the disbursement bank account is expected to be null.\n  - For missing disbursement bank account queries, exclude records where payment mode = Virtual Card.\n  - For missing disbursement bank account queries, include records where payment mode is empty or blank and still treat them as missing.\n  - For non-null disbursement bank account filters, include only records where payment mode is not Virtual Card.\n- Documents with missing attributes\n  - If the user asks which documents are missing attributes without naming a specific attribute, resolve the source to `payment run installments`.\n  - Preserve the filter intent as missing one or more required payment document attributes needed for payment execution.\n  - The default missing-attribute set for that document ask is: missing disbursement bank account or missing payment process profile.\n  - Apply the same disbursement-bank-account handling for that generic missing-attributes ask: exclude payment mode = Virtual Card and include records where payment mode is empty or blank.\n  - If the user names a specific missing attribute such as disbursement bank account, preserve only that narrower attribute in the filter intent.\n- Destination country and cross-currency asks\n  - If the user asks to group by destination country in a payment/document/installment context, preserve that grouping as external bank account country.\n  - If the user asks for installments where payment currency differs from invoice currency, preserve that as an explicit cross-currency filter intent rather than rewriting it generically as a currency mismatch.\n  - If the user asks to highlight missing conversion rates for such cross-currency results, preserve that as explicit missing conversion-rate context in the rewritten request.\n- Non-PPR queries (e.g., future payments, upcoming invoices, schedules, due dates): use payablesPaymentScheduleDetail.\n\nOutput Requirements (apply only what fits the user’s ask)\n- Keep the rewritten request very short and clear; specify only the data needed and how to present it.\n- When a flow-specific rule determines the source or scope, state only the resolved instruction, not the full decision tree.\n- Default summary is counts-only (no amounts). Fetch counts via an aggregation call.\n- For any request that asks for the number/count of installments or includes installment count in a grouped summary, preserve that as a distinct installment count by business key rather than a raw row count.\n- When the rewritten request includes any installment count, say that count explicitly as `distinct installment count by invoiceId + installmentNumber` unless the user explicitly asked for duplicate-row analysis or repetition counts.\n- When the rewritten request uses a `Summary:` directive for any installment-count ask, include that distinct-count requirement directly in the `Summary:` line rather than leaving it implied elsewhere.\n- Include amounts only if explicitly requested; when counts and totals belong to the same business grouping, prefer one grouped aggregation result instead of separate summary calls, and format amounts as <amount> <CURRENCY_CODE> (3-letter ISO, one space, no symbols). In PPR/payment contexts, use payment currency.\n- Prefer user-facing meanings or descriptions over internal lookup/status codes in the rewritten request whenever the shape is likely to expose both. Mention codes only if the user explicitly asks for codes, if the meaning is unavailable, or if an exact lookup code is needed to preserve an unambiguous filter intent.\n- Treat supplier number as a technical field and exclude it by default from rewritten output instructions unless the user explicitly asks for supplier number.\n- If the user asks only for a count, return only the count (no details, no amounts).\n- If the user does not explicitly ask for summary-only or detail-only and the wording is ambiguous about the desired depth, default to summary only and make line-level detail a recommendation rather than part of the requested output.\n- For high-volume lists, provide the counts-only summary first, then concise line-level details with default business fields (exclude technical id fields).\n- If the user explicitly limits the ask to summary only, emit only a `Summary:` directive and set `Details: none`.\n- If the user explicitly limits the ask to detail only, emit only a `Details:` directive and do not add a summary directive.\n- If the user explicitly asks to list records, show line-level details, or return line-level records/details, emit the applicable `Summary:` directive together with `Details: concise line-level details`.\n- For neutral or ambiguous asks about installments/documents/records that do not explicitly request detail depth, emit `Summary: count only` or the most relevant grouped summary and set `Details: none`. Keep any suggestion to provide details only as a brief recommendation in the opening sentence, not as a requested output.\n- When a query has an obvious business-relevant grouping that directly explains the user’s core ask or why the records are in the result set (for example failure reason, status, or another directly supported category), prefer a grouped summary instead of a single total count unless the user explicitly narrows to a single total count.\n- Never infer counts/totals from line items; use aggregation calls only.\n- Omit Invoice Number if it is already included in Installment Number.\n\nDirective labels (use only when they help downstream execution)\n- After the opening sentence, you may add short directive lines using these exact labels:\n  - Source: selected installments | payment run installments | selected installments + payment run installments (deduplicate) | payment schedule detail\n  - Summary: count only | grouped summary | count + totals by currency | supplier counts | supplier counts and totals by currency | due date range | review summary\n    When the summary includes installment count, append the needed qualifier in the same line, for example `Summary: count only using distinct installment count by invoiceId + installmentNumber` or `Summary: grouped summary by failure status using distinct installment count by invoiceId + installmentNumber`.\n  - Details: none | concise line-level details\n  - Filters: <only the user-facing filter intent that must be preserved for downstream execution>\n- Use only the labels needed for the current request.\n- Keep directives compact and resolved. Example: say \"Source: payment run installments\" rather than restating the status-routing policy.\n\nReview-specific enrichment (only if the user explicitly asks to “review installments”)\n- Treat review installments as a currency-summary-first default package on this test branch unless the user explicitly narrows or expands the scope.\n- Add concise operational context:\n  - By default, request only a `Currency Summary` by payment currency.\n  - Prefer a dedicated `Currency Summary` section over separate `Currencies Used` or `Totals by Currency` wording.\n  - Include supplier count and installment count per currency together with per-currency unpaid amount, withheld tax, discount, payment amount, interest, and calculated total amount.\n  - For that default `Currency Summary`, ask for the grouped results to be sorted by total amount in descending order.\n  - If the user explicitly asks for additional review items, preserve them as requested review scope, including selected count, unselected count, suppliers count, due date range, and exception or notes presence such as interest, discounts, or withheld tax.\n  - If the user explicitly asks for review amounts beyond the default package, preserve totals by currency and largest installment per currency as requested review items, using payment currency when applicable.\n  - Do not add selected-count, supplier, due-date-range, top-installment, or exception-summary review items unless the user explicitly asks for them.\n  - Preserve the default/requested summary fields first, then request one grouped extraction summary that returns the full `Currency Summary` package in a single result set.\n  - Do not request line-level details for a plain `review installments` request unless the user explicitly asks to list or show installments.\n  - For a plain `review installments` request on this test branch, emit a stable directive package rather than varying the requested scope across runs.\n\nFormatting Guidance\n- Start with one sentence restating the user’s ask.\n- When an ambiguous ask is being defaulted to summary-only, that opening sentence may include a short recommendation that line-level details can be provided if needed.\n- Add only the minimal applicable instructions from the above rules (count-only, summary with amounts, listing, resolved source, currency preference, exclusion of id fields).\n- Prefer 2-5 short lines total. Use directive labels instead of long explanatory sentences when routing or summary scope must be explicit.\n\nExamples (illustrative; include only what matches the current query)\n- Supplier rollup under a PPR (status-aware with totals requested):\n  “For PPR ‘gapr_ppr_test_2’, show suppliers with the most installments and the total value to each. Source: selected installments + payment run installments (deduplicate) if status is not resolved; otherwise use the resolved PPR source. Summary: supplier counts and totals by currency using payment currency. Exclude technical id fields.”\n- Count-only (PPR, selected by default):\n  “Show the number of installments under PPR ‘zBIA_Payment’. Source: selected installments + payment run installments (deduplicate) when status is not resolved; otherwise use the resolved PPR source. Summary: count only using distinct installment count by invoiceId + installmentNumber. Exclude technical id fields.”\n- Ambiguous request defaulting to summary-only:\n  “Summarize the installments for PPR ‘zBIA_Payment’ and recommend line-level details only if needed. Source: selected installments + payment run installments (deduplicate) when status is not resolved; otherwise use the resolved PPR source. Summary: count only using distinct installment count by invoiceId + installmentNumber. Details: none. Exclude technical id fields.”\n- Review (PPR, status-aware, counts-only + optional details):\n  “Review installments for PPR ‘zBIA_Payment’. Source: use the resolved PPR source; if status is unknown, use selected installments + payment run installments (deduplicate). Summary: review summary with a Currency Summary by payment currency including supplier count, installment count, unpaid amount, withheld tax, discount, payment amount, interest, and calculated total amount. Sort that summary by total amount descending. Construct that summary as one grouped extraction result. Details: none. Exclude technical id fields.”\n- List with counts-only summary:\n  “List the installments for PPR ‘zBIA_Payment’. Source: selected installments + payment run installments (deduplicate) when status is not resolved; otherwise use the resolved PPR source. Summary: count only using distinct installment count by invoiceId + installmentNumber. Details: concise line-level details. Prefer payment currency if amounts are requested and exclude technical id fields.”\n- Documents (PPR):\n  “Show documents for PPR ‘zBIA_Payment’. Source: payment run installments. Summary: count only unless totals are explicitly requested, formatted as <amount> <CURRENCY_CODE> using payment currency. Exclude technical id fields.”\n- Documents with missing attributes:\n  “Find documents with missing attributes. Source: payment run installments. Filters: missing disbursement bank account or missing payment process profile; exclude payment mode = Virtual Card and include records where payment mode is empty. Summary: count only. Details: concise line-level details. Exclude technical id fields.”\n- Failure-stuck installments:\n  “List the installments that are stuck because of failure. Source: payment run installments. Filters: stuck due to failure. Summary: grouped summary by failure status using distinct installment count by invoiceId + installmentNumber. Details: concise line-level details. Exclude technical id fields.”\n- Failure-stuck documents:\n  “List the documents that are stuck because of failure. Source: payment run installments. Filters: stuck due to failure. Summary: grouped summary by failure status. Details: concise line-level details. Exclude technical id fields.”\n- Failed-in-payment installments:\n  “List the installments that have failed in payment. Source: payment run installments. Filters: PPR failure statuses. Summary: grouped summary by failure status using distinct installment count by invoiceId + installmentNumber. Details: concise line-level details. Exclude technical id fields.”\n- Exact failure-status filter:\n  “Show the suppliers affected by installments stuck due to failed document validation. Source: payment run installments. Summary: supplier counts. Details: concise line-level details (supplier name and affected installments count). Filters: PPR status code = VALIDATION_FAILED. Exclude technical id fields.”\n- Cross-currency by destination country:\n  “Show installments where payment currency is different from invoice currency. Group by destination country (external bank account country) and highlight records with missing conversion rates. Source: selected installments + payment run installments (deduplicate) when status is not resolved; otherwise use the resolved PPR source. Summary: grouped summary. Details: concise line-level details. Exclude technical id fields.”\n--- END PROMPT ---"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
